            <div xml:id="d981">

                <pb facs="0750" n="634" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg634"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14084a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 26, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>376. Press despatches announce that the Provisional President has issued an order
                    directing, generals to abstain from summary executions. The President heartily
                    approves the action taken. Please convey this information to General Gutiérrez
                    and if you consider the circumstances favorable urge upon Villa acceptance of
                    this order as best means of strengthening Provisional Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
